or 2022; range = MAX−MIN per dw_1335/dw_2272/dw_3311) | SUPPORTED | SUPPORTED |\n| academic year description | SUPPORTED via ACADEMIC_TERMS(_ALL) join on TERM_CODE (dw_1023, dw_4448) | SUPPORTED via terms | SUPPORTED via terms |\n| library status-'U' population + TOTAL_UNITS | SUPPORTED (lrm has TERM_CODE+SUBJECT_ID; dw_4701 computes AVG/STDDEV of ccso.TOTAL_UNITS for status-'U' reserves; dw_1301/dw_4724 join keys) | NOT the precedent source for library-reserve unit stats | NOT used in any library precedent |\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring**\n- \"degree-granting subjects\" → course-level `SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'` (precedents dw_3163 \"the course is degree granting\", dw_1049 \"are degree-granting\" both anchor here); it excludes the department-level reading `SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` (dw_2151's \"department that grants degrees\" wording differs from ours). Discriminating fact if challenged: whether the count threshold is evaluated per course-flag population (dw_1049) — our wording \"degree-granting **subjects**\" matches the course-flag reading lexically.\n- \"offered in 2022\" → `COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022` per `column_concept_year_columns` decision guide and dw_1049/dw_2151/dw_104/dw_3493.\n- \"if at least 5\" → `HAVING COUNT(*) >= 5` (dw_1049 uses `> 5` for \"more than five\"; ours says \"at least 5\").\n- \"library reserve materials … material status 'U'\" → `LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL.LIBRARY_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'U'` (documented value domain; `column_concept_material_status_key` distinguishes it from TIP's 'U').\n- \"coefficient of variation (using STDDEV only…)\" → `STDDEV(x)/NULLIF(AVG(x),0)` exactly as dw_2180; per system tip, bare `STDDEV()` is written.\n- \"academic year description\" → `ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC` (exists only in ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence**\n- 2022 + degree-granting + count-threshold + catalog units: 1 direct precedent (dw_1049, on COURSE_